Kamen Fight - Project Documentation
====================================

Kamen Fight is a Web-based, turn-based Kamen Rider fighting game built with vanilla JavaScript (ES6+), HTML5 Video, and CSS3. 
The game features simultaneous command selection, directional charge mechanics, sequential video-driven combat resolution, deterministic PRNG-based mechanics, multi-threaded Expectimax & Monte Carlo lookahead AI engines, headless batch simulation with replay verification, and full mirror-match support.

Key Features & Architecture
---------------------------
* Directional Charge System: Players hold directional keys (W, A, S, D) to build charge percentages prior to confirming attacks with action keys (I, J, K, L). Charge levels dynamically scale attack damage, accuracy, priority, and guard effectiveness.
* Decoupled Deterministic Combat Core: Pure state-machine combat resolution engine (js/combat_core.js) supporting deterministic state resolution, seedable Mulberry32 PRNG, outcome probability enumeration, and side-swapping spatial symmetry.
* Advanced Multi-Threaded AI: Decision search pipeline utilizing parallel Web Workers, Depth-1 Expectimax evaluation, character-specific tactical heuristics (js/rider_brains.js), opponent habit decay models, and deep multi-turn Monte Carlo horizon rollouts (js/foresee_engine.js).
* Resource & Stun Mechanics: Chi resource pool capped at 16 with dynamic Low Power (<5 Chi) debuffs and Full Power (>14 Chi) status bonuses. Faint buildup (100-point threshold) forces targets into a 1-turn stunned idle state.
* Headless Batch Simulator & Replay Verifier: Fast background Monte Carlo simulation engine (js/simulator.js) for CPU vs. CPU balancing (10 to 100+ runs) with strict bit-identical state replay verification (verifyReplay).
* Automated Testing Dashboard: On-screen browser testing suite (test_dashboard.html / js/combat_tests.js) verifying combat rules, state immutability, interrupt logic, and AI difficulty performance.

Project Directory Structure
---------------------------
├── index.html              # Playable game entry point & dynamic view mounting
├── index_test.html     # Automated browser test dashboard & AI benchmark harness
├── css/
│   └── style.css           # Layouts, HUD overlays, bar tracks, video containers, popups
├── data/
│   ├── moves.json          # Master move database, Chi costs, damage ratios, video mappings
│   └── riders.json         # Roster list, base stats (LP, orientation), video folders
├── js/
│   ├── ai.js               # AI decision runner & rolling 24-turn match memory store
│   ├── ai_worker.js        # Background Web Worker thread for parallel AI search
│   ├── combat_core.js      # Decoupled deterministic combat rules & state resolution
│   ├── combat_engine.js    # Live combat playback adapter & visual event orchestrator
│   ├── combat_tests.js     # Automated unit test suite & difficulty benchmark harness
│   ├── common.js           # Utilities, Mulberry32 PRNG, FNV-1a hash, JSON loader
│   ├── cpu_controller.js   # Asynchronous Web Worker pool dispatcher & CPU manager
│   ├── foresee_engine.js   # Expectimax decision search & Monte Carlo horizon rollouts
│   ├── game.js             # Main game lifecycle manager, screen router & HUD painter
│   ├── match_manager.js    # Live input handlers (WASD/Touch), charge monitors, timers
│   ├── media.js            # Video player, mobile video/audio unlocker, sprite flipper
│   ├── rider_brains.js     # Character-specific tactical intelligence profiles & priors
│   ├── simulator.js        # Headless batch simulation engine & replay verifier
│   ├── storage.js          # LocalStorage persistence manager
│   ├── ui.js               # Battle HUD renderer, LP/Chi/Faint bars, damage popups
│   └── vs_select.js        # 3-step character select wizard, BGM manager, sim modal UI
└── assets/
    ├── sounds/             # BGM tracks (matchup.mp3, matchup1.mp3, etc.)
    ├── images/icons/       # Rider thumbnail icons
    └── videos/             # Rider video cutscenes (idle.mp4, faint.mp4, etc.)

Setup & Deployment Instructions
-------------------------------
Local Execution:
To run locally, execute through a local HTTP web server (e.g., Python `python -m http.server`, Node `npx serve`, or VS Code Live Server) to support Web Worker multi-threading and `fetch()` requests for local JSON data files.

GitHub Pages Deployment:
Push the repository to GitHub and enable GitHub Pages under Settings > Pages.

Asset Naming Warning:
Ensure all asset paths and video filenames inside assets/videos/<rider_id>/ are strictly lowercase (e.g., idle.mp4, guard.mp4) to prevent 404 case-sensitivity errors on Linux production hosts.

Automated Testing & AI Benchmarking:
Open `test_dashboard.html` in any browser to execute the 15-point combat rule assertion suite (`runCombatTests`) and run head-to-head AI difficulty benchmarks (`benchmarkDifficulties`).



